1
00:00:07,921 --> 00:00:13,084
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,365 --> 00:00:15,438
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:21,564
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:21,949 --> 00:00:25,878
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

5
00:00:26,632 --> 00:00:31,299
رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِي صَدْرِي۝وَيَسِّرْ لِي أَمْرِي۝وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِنْ لِسَانِي۝يَفْقَهُوا قَوْلِي۝

6
00:00:31,554 --> 00:00:33,253
السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

7
00:00:33,278 --> 00:00:34,328
To all the listeners.

8
00:00:35,181 --> 00:00:37,162
Before we start with the Battle of Uhud(اُحَدْ)

9
00:00:37,665 --> 00:00:44,509
a few scattered Ghazawaat(غزوات) and Saraya(سراية) that occurred after Badr(بدر) and before Uhud(اُحَدْ).

10
00:00:44,855 --> 00:00:47,502
One of them is Ghazwat Ma-Qadar(غزوة ما قدر)

11
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:52,511
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), seven days after the Battle of Badr(بدر).

12
00:00:53,172 --> 00:00:55,160
The Muslims were already on the road.

13
00:00:55,721 --> 00:01:04,087
They went to attack this was a preemptive attack on Bannu Sulaim(بنوسليم).

14
00:01:04,245 --> 00:01:08,404
 Bannu Sulaim(بنوسليم), a tribe Rasool Allah ﷺ caught word

15
00:01:08,492 --> 00:01:14,343
that they were gathering to attack Madina, so Rasool Allah ﷺ attacked them first.

16
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:20,182
This was something that repeats throughout the Ghazawat(غزوات) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

17
00:01:20,258 --> 00:01:24,742
 he hears that people are plotting to attack Madina,

18
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:32,331
so he starts first and takes the initiative and takes advantage of the surprise attack.

19
00:01:34,076 --> 00:01:37,456
And they surprised Bannu Sulaim(بنوسليم),

20
00:01:37,536 --> 00:01:41,419
so Bannu Sulaim(بنوسليم) fled the scene and they left behind 500 camels

21
00:01:41,487 --> 00:01:47,220
which ended up being a good booty for the Muslims, each soldier ended up getting about two camels

22
00:01:48,138 --> 00:01:50,188
and they went back to Madina.

23
00:01:51,493 --> 00:01:53,800
There was another Ghazwa(غزوة) called Ghazwat As-Suwaik(غزوةإلسويق).

24
00:01:55,792 --> 00:02:02,931
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان), trying to wash away the shame of Badr(بدر), goes to Bannu Nadhir(بنو نضير),

25
00:02:03,050 --> 00:02:05,228
 the Jewish tribe of Bannu Nadhir(بنو نضير).

26
00:02:05,982 --> 00:02:11,318
They stay as guests of Salam Bin Mashkam(سلام بن مشكم), the head of Bannu Nadhir(بنو نضير).

27
00:02:12,024 --> 00:02:16,747
And they get some valuable information from him, some insider information.

28
00:02:17,623 --> 00:02:22,776
And they attack the outskirts of Madina, they find over there two Muslims, they killed them,

29
00:02:23,154 --> 00:02:26,590
they destroy the area just took some stuff with him and left.

30
00:02:27,543 --> 00:02:32,318
So, it wasn't much of revenge for Badr(بدر).

31
00:02:33,661 --> 00:02:39,871
Rasool Allah ﷺ heard about it and he immediately pursued them with 200 soldiers.

32
00:02:40,927 --> 00:02:44,448
And Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) had 200 soldiers with him too

33
00:02:44,936 --> 00:02:46,079
but he was running away.

34
00:02:46,603 --> 00:02:48,013
 And they were so terrified.

35
00:02:48,631 --> 00:02:52,576
They were throwing their food stuff,

36
00:02:52,726 --> 00:02:55,607
this is particular kind of food that they will take with them.

37
00:02:56,072 --> 00:02:58,388
It's kind of food that doesn't spoil, it's called Suwaik(سويق).

38
00:02:59,217 --> 00:03:05,202
Apparently it's some grains and it's mixed with butter or honey

39
00:03:05,707 --> 00:03:10,675
and they would carry it with them and since its expiration date is very late,

40
00:03:11,106 --> 00:03:13,277
it's pretty good food for fighters.

41
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:20,122
So, they were throwing away this food to lighten the load and they ran away.

42
00:03:20,216 --> 00:03:24,091
So no fighting occurred in Ghazwat As-Suwaik(غزوة إلسويق).

43
00:03:25,645 --> 00:03:29,409
In another Ghazwa(غزوة), Ghazwat Ghimr(غزوة الغمر) four Hundred and fifty(450) Muslims.

44
00:03:30,973 --> 00:03:33,916
And this was against a tribe in Najd(نجد).

45
00:03:34,586 --> 00:03:39,741
And Rasool Allah ﷺ attack them because he heard that they were planning to attack him.

46
00:03:40,863 --> 00:03:43,011
So, he goes to meet them in their own territory.

47
00:03:43,516 --> 00:03:49,801
On the way he arrests one of their men called Jabbar Bin Thalaba(جبار بن ثالبه), who becomes Muslim.

48
00:03:50,749 --> 00:03:54,577
And then when they reached to the enemy's land,

49
00:03:55,968 --> 00:04:00,021
it was rainy, so the cloths of Rasool Allah ﷺ got wet,

50
00:04:00,727 --> 00:04:05,113
so Rasool Allah ﷺ took off his armor and hanged it on a tree,

51
00:04:05,639 --> 00:04:09,775
so that his clothes could dry and then he laid down under a tree.

52
00:04:10,759 --> 00:04:13,226
So, Ja'soor(جعثور), the head of the

53
00:04:13,832 --> 00:04:15,565
enemy's army sneaked in,

54
00:04:16,270 --> 00:04:21,379
and he stood right above Rasool Allah ﷺ with his sword in hand.

55
00:04:22,183 --> 00:04:25,216
And while Rasool Allah ﷺ was sleeping, he woke him up and said,

56
00:04:25,642 --> 00:04:26,920
O Muhammad(محمد)

57
00:04:27,285 --> 00:04:29,212
مَنْ يَمْنَعُكَ مِنِّيْ الْآنْ

58
00:04:29,651 --> 00:04:31,712
Who can save you from me now?

59
00:04:33,311 --> 00:04:35,825
Rasool Allah ﷺ with all confidence, said: Allah.

60
00:04:36,987 --> 00:04:43,137
Suddenly Ja'soor(جعثور) falls back and his sword fell.

61
00:04:43,802 --> 00:04:48,454
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ picks up the sword and stands on top of Ja'soor(جعثور) and says;

62
00:04:48,494 --> 00:04:51,779
 Ya Ja'soor(يا جعثور)! Who can protect you from me now?

63
00:04:54,065 --> 00:04:58,512
So, he pleads to Rasool Allah ﷺ to spare him, his life.

64
00:04:59,618 --> 00:05:01,308
 And he became Muslim.

65
00:05:03,471 --> 00:05:05,778
He goes back to his people and his people blame him, they said,

66
00:05:05,803 --> 00:05:07,628
what's your problem, what's happened to you?

67
00:05:07,668 --> 00:05:11,784
He said; A tall man stood in front of me and pushed me in my chest.

68
00:05:12,590 --> 00:05:14,004
And that was Jibreel عليه السّلام.

69
00:05:15,127 --> 00:05:18,103
So, Ja'soor(جعثور), who wanted to kill Rasool Allah ﷺ becomes Muslim.

70
00:05:18,445 --> 00:05:21,804
He goes back gives his people Da'wah(دعوة) many of them become Muslim,

71
00:05:23,283 --> 00:05:27,481
a miracle, of the miracles of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

72
00:05:30,281 --> 00:05:33,629
But this was a one month long journey,

73
00:05:34,923 --> 00:05:36,851
I mean they were absent for an entire month.

74
00:05:37,639 --> 00:05:39,648
And then there is a Sariyya(سرية), Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه).

75
00:05:39,718 --> 00:05:43,248
So, this is a Sariyya(سرية), Rasool Allah ﷺ didn't go with them, to Kiradah(كردة).

76
00:05:44,108 --> 00:05:51,760
 The people of Quraish(قريش), were now suffering economically, because of the continuous raids.

77
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:57,121
The Muslims were putting some serious pressure on Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) by raiding their caravans.

78
00:05:57,212 --> 00:06:02,412
 I mean, now the route from Makkah to Syria was jeopardized.

79
00:06:02,857 --> 00:06:04,690
The Muslims are all over the place,

80
00:06:05,379 --> 00:06:08,713
either their armies or tribes loyal to them,

81
00:06:08,753 --> 00:06:11,680
because Rasool Allah ﷺ was sending out these Sarayya(سراية),

82
00:06:12,365 --> 00:06:16,581
to engage with the tribes surrounding Madina to invite them to Islam

83
00:06:16,621 --> 00:06:24,221
or to at least make some alliances with them, to guarantee that they would stand on the Muslim side.

84
00:06:25,251 --> 00:06:29,446
So, now Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), her line to Syria was threatened.

85
00:06:29,983 --> 00:06:32,802
So, they were consulting with some guides and they told them that

86
00:06:32,905 --> 00:06:37,318
well, if the roots of Hijaz(حجاز) are not safe. Why don't we go through Najd(نجد).?

87
00:06:37,711 --> 00:06:42,498
So, they're going to take this long turn through Najd(نجد), getting close to Iraq(عراق),

88
00:06:42,566 --> 00:06:45,792
 and then from there, they're going to enter into Syria

89
00:06:46,886 --> 00:06:53,732
which obviously costs more and takes longer but they had to do, what they had to do.

90
00:06:54,514 --> 00:06:59,192
So, they sent this caravan to go through Najd(نجد) and from Iraq and then into Syria.

91
00:07:00,105 --> 00:07:06,343
And Rasool Allah ﷺ sends out Sariyya(سرية) led by Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) and a 100 Muslims to raid it.

92
00:07:07,225 --> 00:07:09,061
This just drove them crazy.

93
00:07:09,429 --> 00:07:12,105
And it was a successful attack.

94
00:07:12,698 --> 00:07:15,980
The guards of the caravan ran away.

95
00:07:17,024 --> 00:07:23,862
And the Muslims took over the caravan says it had so much silver in it.

96
00:07:25,878 --> 00:07:34,911
Now these skirmishes or small battles and Ghazawaat(غزوات) served few objectives of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

97
00:07:35,824 --> 00:07:38,237
First of all there were hands on military training

98
00:07:39,943 --> 00:07:45,498
Number two, and this issue of military training is Ibadah(عبادة) in itself.

99
00:07:45,538 --> 00:07:46,336
 Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

100
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:48,053
وَأَعِدُّوا لَهُمْ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ مِنْ قُوَّةٍ

101
00:07:48,093 --> 00:07:50,125
Prepare whatever strength you can.

102
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:56,138
So, any training that could help the Muslim in Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) is Ibadah(عبادة).

103
00:07:56,202 --> 00:07:59,802
It's just like praying" fasting, paying Zakah(زكواة), it's Ibadah(عبادة).

104
00:08:00,703 --> 00:08:04,978
And if Jihad(جهاد) is Fardh(فرض) then the preparation becomes Fardh(فرض) too.

105
00:08:05,491 --> 00:08:08,090
So, they were worshiping Allahعَزّوجَلّ through this training.

106
00:08:08,232 --> 00:08:09,547
 It was hands on military training,

107
00:08:09,626 --> 00:08:14,975
it wasn't in a military school or it was in the field, actual training.

108
00:08:15,819 --> 00:08:17,943
Number two, it's Tarbiyyah(تربية).

109
00:08:19,135 --> 00:08:22,850
Because the Sahabah(صحابه) would spend long time with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

110
00:08:22,930 --> 00:08:27,875
 So, for example, in the Ghazwa(غزوة) that we just talked about, they were absent for an entire month.

111
00:08:28,277 --> 00:08:30,897
So, they were spending this time with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

112
00:08:31,922 --> 00:08:36,418
traveling with him, eating with him, walking with him,

113
00:08:36,839 --> 00:08:44,577
 and you get exposed to some aspects of a person's personality in travel,

114
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:49,393
 that you might not be exposed to, if a person is residing in their home,

115
00:08:49,901 --> 00:08:55,949
because the mixing and mingling, when you are traveling with somebody is more.

116
00:08:56,652 --> 00:09:02,262
So, the Sahabah(صحابه) get to see the personality of Rasool Allah ﷺ in front of their eyes

117
00:09:02,302 --> 00:09:06,151
 and this is how they learned the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

118
00:09:06,524 --> 00:09:08,849
 So, they would learn about his Ibadah(عبادة)

119
00:09:09,024 --> 00:09:13,952
and they would also, the third benefit of these Ghazawaat(غزوات) Is.

120
00:09:13,992 --> 00:09:16,937
 It teaches the Muslim how to be a member of a group of a Jama'a(جماعة).

121
00:09:17,505 --> 00:09:22,902
Because there is Samman Ta'ah (سمعا طاعة) there is obedience, there is discipline, there is sacrifice,

122
00:09:23,017 --> 00:09:26,398
 because you know, you are part of a group, you're not just an individual doing your own thing.

123
00:09:26,734 --> 00:09:34,838
So, these are habits that they get to learn by traveling for such long extended periods, with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

124
00:09:34,909 --> 00:09:40,035
so it was also a Tarbiyyah(تربية) for them, and how to be part of the Ummah(أمة)

125
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:45,543
because Islam is not individualistic religion, it's a collective religion,

126
00:09:45,622 --> 00:09:47,921
a lot of the Ibadaat(عبادات) in Islam are done collectively,

127
00:09:48,318 --> 00:09:49,683
Salah(صلاة) is done collectively,

128
00:09:51,273 --> 00:09:53,730
Hajj(حج) is done collectively, Umrah(عمره) is done collectively,

129
00:09:54,316 --> 00:09:56,409
Jihad(جهاد) most of the time is done collectively.

130
00:09:56,950 --> 00:10:02,182
So, all of these Ibadaat(عبادات), that they get to learn from Rasool Allah ﷺ in the field.

131
00:10:03,673 --> 00:10:05,570
We move on to the Battle of Uhud(اُحَدْ),

132
00:10:06,294 --> 00:10:08,548
what were the reasons for the Battle of Uhud(اُحَدْ)?

133
00:10:08,619 --> 00:10:12,913
There were religious reasons, economical reasons, political reasons and social reasons.

134
00:10:13,991 --> 00:10:15,468
The religious reason,

135
00:10:16,032 --> 00:10:19,659
the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) wanted to stop the advance of Islam.

136
00:10:20,210 --> 00:10:22,697
They wanted to stand between the people and becoming Muslim.

137
00:10:23,083 --> 00:10:24,340
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

138
00:10:24,998 --> 00:10:34,346
إِنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا يُنْفِقُونَ أَمْوَالَهُمْ لِيَصُدُّوا عَنْ سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ۚ

139
00:10:34,806 --> 00:10:43,244
فَسَيُنْفِقُونَهَا ثُمَّ تَكُونُ عَلَيْهِمْ حَسْرَةً ثُمَّ يُغْلَبُونَ ۗ

140
00:10:43,697 --> 00:10:50,268
وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا إِلَىٰ جَهَنَّمَ يُحْشَرُونَ۝

141
00:10:50,451 --> 00:10:56,170
Indeed, those who disbelieve spend their wealth to avert people from the way of Allah.

142
00:10:56,822 --> 00:10:57,949
So they will spend it,

143
00:10:58,329 --> 00:11:01,229
then it will be for them a source of regret,

144
00:11:01,909 --> 00:11:03,651
then they will be overcome.

145
00:11:03,941 --> 00:11:08,145
And those who have disbelieved on to hell they will be gathered.

146
00:11:08,598 --> 00:11:12,460
So, it says here that they're spending their wealth to avert people from the way of Allah.

147
00:11:13,449 --> 00:11:14,331
At-Tabri(ألطبري) says;

148
00:11:14,566 --> 00:11:18,544
يَصْرِفُوْنَ اَمْوَالَهُمْ وَيُنْفِقُوْنَهَا لْيَمْنَعُ النَّاسَ مِنْ دُخُوْلِ الْاِسْلَامْ

149
00:11:19,327 --> 00:11:22,248
They're spending their money to prevent people from becoming Muslim.

150
00:11:22,705 --> 00:11:24,333
And Ash-Shoukani(ألشوكاني) says about this Ayah(آية),

151
00:11:24,605 --> 00:11:33,743
وَالْمَعْنَى اَنَّ غَرَضَ هَا اُوْلآءِ الْكُفَّارْ فِيْ اَنْفَاقِ اَمْوَالِهِمْ هُوَّ صَدُّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ الله بِمُحَارَبَةِ رَسُول الله وَجَمْعِ الْجُيُوْشِ لِذَالِكْ

152
00:11:35,178 --> 00:11:39,060
The meaning, is that the objective of these Kuffar(كفار) in spending their money,

153
00:11:39,706 --> 00:11:44,054
is to stand between the people and becoming Muslim, by fighting Rasool Allah ﷺ

154
00:11:44,349 --> 00:11:47,957
and mobilizing armies, for that purpose.

155
00:11:48,782 --> 00:11:51,000
And history is repeating itself,

156
00:11:51,775 --> 00:11:57,417
look at how much money, the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ are spending to fight Islam

157
00:11:57,497 --> 00:11:59,657
billions of dollars are spent for that

158
00:12:00,444 --> 00:12:04,592
to kill the Ouleaa(أوليآء) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, to around them up, to capture them

159
00:12:04,942 --> 00:12:07,497
and to tarnish the reputation of Islam,

160
00:12:07,658 --> 00:12:10,515
lots of money is spent for that purpose.

161
00:12:10,815 --> 00:12:15,489
So, the kuffar(كفار) of today are not very different from the kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

162
00:12:17,455 --> 00:12:19,481
The social reason,

163
00:12:20,066 --> 00:12:22,550
Quraish(قريش) wanted to wash away the shame of Badr(بدر).

164
00:12:23,221 --> 00:12:27,962
That was a serious dent in the reputation and they wanted to make up for that.

165
00:12:28,596 --> 00:12:29,846
The economical reason,

166
00:12:30,558 --> 00:12:35,408
we talked about how those raids were putting serious pressure on the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

167
00:12:36,044 --> 00:12:44,413
who were accustomed to having all the Arabs respect them, and opened the way for them, to both Yemen and Syria.

168
00:12:44,878 --> 00:12:45,920
But now things are different

169
00:12:48,154 --> 00:12:49,349
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

170
00:12:50,010 --> 00:12:53,069
لِإِيلَافِ قُرَيْشٍ۝

171
00:12:53,412 --> 00:12:59,474
إِيلَافِهِمْ رِحْلَةَ الشِّتَاءِ وَالصَّيْفِ ۝

172
00:12:59,839 --> 00:13:04,077
 فَلْيَعْبُدُوا رَبَّ هَٰذَا الْبَيْتِ ۝

173
00:13:04,553 --> 00:13:14,786
الَّذِي أَطْعَمَهُمْ مِنْ جُوعٍ وَآمَنَهُمْ مِنْ خَوْفٍ۝

174
00:13:16,327 --> 00:13:19,826
For the accustomed security of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they were accustomed to security.

175
00:13:20,479 --> 00:13:24,282
Their accustomed security, in the caravan of winter and summer.

176
00:13:24,968 --> 00:13:28,576
The caravan of winter was to Yemen and the caravan of summer was to Syria.

177
00:13:29,239 --> 00:13:32,988
Let them worship, the Lord of this house, who has fed them,

178
00:13:33,154 --> 00:13:35,813
 saving them from hunger and made them safe,

179
00:13:36,256 --> 00:13:37,556
saving them from fear,

180
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:40,053
but because they refused to worship Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

181
00:13:40,383 --> 00:13:42,681
Now that accustomed security was gone.

182
00:13:44,959 --> 00:13:51,697
Now only one leg of their journey was affected, and that is from Makkah to Syria.

183
00:13:51,769 --> 00:13:55,683
Because they had two Journeys, one was from Makkah to Yemen and Abyssinia

184
00:13:56,032 --> 00:13:58,014
the second one was from Makkah to Syria.

185
00:13:58,455 --> 00:14:01,152
The journey of Syria was done in summer

186
00:14:01,205 --> 00:14:03,817
and the journey to Yemen and Abyssinia was in winter.

187
00:14:04,961 --> 00:14:13,592
However, cutting the route to Syria affects also the route to Yemen,

188
00:14:13,632 --> 00:14:14,305
Why?

189
00:14:14,573 --> 00:14:19,600
Because the business of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) was based on buying products from Yemen

190
00:14:20,133 --> 00:14:22,652
and selling them in Syria and vice versa.

191
00:14:23,298 --> 00:14:26,381
So, since now they are having difficulty going to Syria,

192
00:14:26,865 --> 00:14:33,703
that will also affect their business in Yemen because they end up selling those products of Syria in Yemen.

193
00:14:34,418 --> 00:14:36,227
So, Safwaan Ibn Ummayyah(صفوان ابن امية) says;

194
00:14:37,339 --> 00:14:40,087
Muhammad(محمد) and his companions have ruined our trade,

195
00:14:40,908 --> 00:14:45,007
while we do not know, what measures to take against them, we are at lost,

196
00:14:45,745 --> 00:14:49,562
they are constantly threatening the coastal area,

197
00:14:49,849 --> 00:14:53,529
while its inhabitants are either at peace or alliance with him.

198
00:14:54,231 --> 00:14:55,243
Where shall we live?

199
00:14:55,566 --> 00:14:56,747
And where should we stay?

200
00:14:57,054 --> 00:14:59,030
If we stay here in our hometown,

201
00:14:59,497 --> 00:15:03,407
we will be forced to eat from our capital, which will soon be consumed

202
00:15:03,751 --> 00:15:07,387
we depend for our lives on trade with Syria in the summer

203
00:15:07,862 --> 00:15:10,020
and with Yemen and Abyssinia in winter.

204
00:15:10,449 --> 00:15:13,694
So, Muhammadﷺ was squeezing Makkah tight,

205
00:15:14,894 --> 00:15:16,262
they were feeling suffocated.

206
00:15:16,848 --> 00:15:20,762
And this shows you the strategy of Rasool Allah ﷺ

207
00:15:21,092 --> 00:15:28,618
of not only afflicting physical harm at Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), in actual warfare, battles on the battle ground,

208
00:15:28,929 --> 00:15:34,626
but also giving attention to the economical war against Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

209
00:15:35,213 --> 00:15:41,330
which was an important part of the strategy of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

210
00:15:43,153 --> 00:15:46,764
And then you have the political reason, the status of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) was shaken.

211
00:15:47,099 --> 00:15:52,557
You know, this outstanding victory of the Muslims,

212
00:15:53,190 --> 00:15:59,202
seriously weakened the reputation of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) in Arabia,

213
00:16:00,296 --> 00:16:03,928
which was seen as the noble most respected tribe.

214
00:16:04,705 --> 00:16:06,975
You don't fight against Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), you respect them.

215
00:16:07,344 --> 00:16:13,350
So, now all of this was changing the status quo was not the status quo anymore.

216
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:18,772
So, they wanted to regain their reputation again.

217
00:16:19,269 --> 00:16:20,616
So, there was a political reason.

218
00:16:21,809 --> 00:16:25,001
So, Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) assembles an army 3000 strong

219
00:16:25,357 --> 00:16:30,648
and they financed that army from the caravan, which Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) saved.

220
00:16:31,079 --> 00:16:33,052
The one that was the cause for the Battle of Badr(بدر).

221
00:16:33,156 --> 00:16:34,568
You remembered that caravan.

222
00:16:34,902 --> 00:16:42,908
This caravan its entire wealth, everything in that Caravan was used to finance the Battle of Uhud(اُحَدْ).

223
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:51,741
Rasool Allah ﷺ is constantly receiving information, he has spies all over.

224
00:16:52,343 --> 00:16:57,541
Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب) now is working for Rasool Allah ﷺ in Makkah.

225
00:16:58,113 --> 00:17:03,291
So, he sends a message to Rasool Allah ﷺ, which was carried swiftly in three days,

226
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:08,566
which is impressive for the modes of transportation in those days

227
00:17:08,973 --> 00:17:13,150
to cut the distance between Makkah and Madina in three days. That's pretty good, it's fast.

228
00:17:14,154 --> 00:17:18,378
So, a letter is conveyed to Rasool Allah ﷺ telling him the details,

229
00:17:19,244 --> 00:17:20,415
an army of 3000.

230
00:17:21,061 --> 00:17:22,711
They have 700 coat males,

231
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:25,933
they have such and such, number of camels.

232
00:17:26,361 --> 00:17:28,617
So, he was being elaborate in the details.

233
00:17:29,065 --> 00:17:34,002
So, this is the first news that reaches Rasool Allah ﷺ of the plans of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

234
00:17:34,585 --> 00:17:39,626
And the source of this information was Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib رضي الله عنه.

235
00:17:41,304 --> 00:17:43,592
When the news was delivered to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

236
00:17:43,956 --> 00:17:48,319
he told Ubaye Bin Ka'ab(أبيئ بن كعب), who read the letter, keep this secret.

237
00:17:49,065 --> 00:17:50,241
Don't tell anybody about it.

238
00:17:51,225 --> 00:17:57,033
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ sends Al-Mundhir(ألمنذر), to go and blend in within the army and get him information.

239
00:17:57,112 --> 00:18:02,687
So, he comes back with the same details which were narrated by Al-Abbas(العباس).

240
00:18:02,727 --> 00:18:07,332
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is collaborating the information from more than one source.

241
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:10,963
And then he sends out Anas(انس) and Muanus(مؤنس)

242
00:18:11,689 --> 00:18:16,479
same thing, to go inside the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and bring in news

243
00:18:16,897 --> 00:18:18,698
and they come back and same thing.

244
00:18:20,059 --> 00:18:26,735
Now Rasool Allah ﷺ then goes to one of the chiefs of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), Saad Ibn Rabiyyah(سعد إبن ربيعة).

245
00:18:27,242 --> 00:18:29,137
He visits him at his house.

246
00:18:30,141 --> 00:18:33,093
And he tells him that Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) is attacking us.

247
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:36,388
He gives him some of the details.

248
00:18:37,029 --> 00:18:38,678
And he gets his opinion.

249
00:18:39,464 --> 00:18:42,731
And he then before he leaves, he tells him keep this secret,

250
00:18:43,140 --> 00:18:45,598
keep this information secret, it classified.

251
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:53,846
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ leaves, the wife of Saad Ibn Rabiyyah(سعد إبن ربيعة) comes to him and says;

252
00:18:54,296 --> 00:18:56,431
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ tell you?

253
00:18:57,257 --> 00:18:58,875
He tells her; it's none of your business.

254
00:18:59,755 --> 00:19:04,076
She said, Well, Rasool Allah ﷺ told you this and that because I heard him,

255
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:06,551
Saad Ibn Rabiyyah(سعد إبن ربيعة) said:

256
00:19:06,654 --> 00:19:09,454
 إِنَّا لِلّهِ وَإِنَّا إِلَيْهِ رَاجِعونَ

257
00:19:09,693 --> 00:19:11,495
This is what you say when a disaster happens.

258
00:19:12,229 --> 00:19:14,373
And then he goes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and tells him,

259
00:19:14,783 --> 00:19:16,001
My wife knows about it.

260
00:19:16,449 --> 00:19:20,549
And I came to tell you that if, just in case the information gets out,

261
00:19:20,998 --> 00:19:23,360
I don't want you to think that I'm the one who leaked it.

262
00:19:25,291 --> 00:19:26,575
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him

263
00:19:26,615 --> 00:19:27,408
 خَلِّيْ عَنْهَا

264
00:19:27,448 --> 00:19:28,300
Leave her alone.

265
00:19:28,748 --> 00:19:32,665
Now we learned from this that a secret is a secret.

266
00:19:32,784 --> 00:19:34,705
 You don't have to tell it, to anyone.

267
00:19:35,730 --> 00:19:38,007
Saad Ibn Rabiyyah(سعد إبن ربيعة) refused to tell it to his own wife.

268
00:19:38,793 --> 00:19:42,790
And he made it very clear, I'm not going to tell you, it's none of your business.

269
00:19:43,863 --> 00:19:52,387
And in such issues relating to the security of the Muslims and military operations.

270
00:19:53,232 --> 00:19:56,831
Rasool Allah ﷺ would function with the Sahabah(صحابه) on a need to know basis.

271
00:19:57,615 --> 00:20:01,762
And somebody who doesn't have to know this information doesn't have to know it.

272
00:20:02,469 --> 00:20:05,408
So, Saad Ibn Rabiyyah(سعد إبن ربيعة) just because, this is his wife,

273
00:20:06,015 --> 00:20:08,749
didn't go and tell her; well Rasool Allah ﷺ told me this and that,

274
00:20:09,291 --> 00:20:13,945
he wasn't trying to impress his wife that Rasool Allah ﷺ came to me and told me about it.

275
00:20:14,731 --> 00:20:20,589
He wasn't being trusting of anyone to give them this information.

276
00:20:21,355 --> 00:20:24,493
And I'm stressing on this point, because many times,

277
00:20:24,827 --> 00:20:28,428
we just assume that because we trust a particular person, we can tell them everything.

278
00:20:29,453 --> 00:20:32,206
If this information is a trust,

279
00:20:33,269 --> 00:20:38,166
it's an Amana(امانة), with you, then you have to treat it as such. It's an Amana(امانة)..

280
00:20:38,845 --> 00:20:43,991
And if somebody tells you the secret and you go and talk about it, then you have, you're being dishonest.

281
00:20:44,196 --> 00:20:45,035
خَيَانَة الْاَمَانَهْ

282
00:20:45,829 --> 00:20:46,824
not keeping the trust.

283
00:20:47,165 --> 00:20:54,745
Also, I want to add that a husband is inclined to tell his wife about everything, that's not right.

284
00:20:55,883 --> 00:21:01,986
Some issues need to be kept away from the closest of your relatives,

285
00:21:02,769 --> 00:21:07,503
parents, wife, children, because again, this is an Amana(امانة).

286
00:21:08,581 --> 00:21:13,048
Now, I hope that my sisters won't be offended by what I've just said.

287
00:21:13,518 --> 00:21:18,534
But emotions sometimes can affect a person male or female.

288
00:21:19,445 --> 00:21:23,810
However, the makeup of females is that they are more emotional than men.

289
00:21:23,850 --> 00:21:27,266
This is not the case in every situation.

290
00:21:27,615 --> 00:21:29,438
We're talking about the majority.

291
00:21:30,698 --> 00:21:37,897
And sisters, the wife would be quite upset that her husband is keeping away information from her sometimes.

292
00:21:39,004 --> 00:21:41,596
But you need to understand the context of the situation

293
00:21:41,625 --> 00:21:45,086
that it was something that is regarding the security of the nation

294
00:21:45,462 --> 00:21:46,333
of the Muslim Ummah(امة).

295
00:21:47,238 --> 00:21:54,244
And I hope that, also the brothers wouldn't take these words and abuse them

296
00:21:54,800 --> 00:21:59,233
and try to keep away information that the wife needs to know.

297
00:22:00,552 --> 00:22:03,910
So, I hope that this is not taken out of context.

298
00:22:04,688 --> 00:22:11,645
Rasool Allah ﷺ holds a Shura(شورى), meeting with the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, on what to do.

299
00:22:12,335 --> 00:22:15,589
So now it's about time to tell the Muslims about what's happening.

300
00:22:16,390 --> 00:22:19,989
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ gathers them and asks them,

301
00:22:20,537 --> 00:22:21,356
what do they think?

302
00:22:22,248 --> 00:22:23,361
There were two opinions.

303
00:22:24,235 --> 00:22:27,229
One, we should fight within Madina

304
00:22:28,260 --> 00:22:37,430
and use it as a fortress and fight in the streets.

305
00:22:38,287 --> 00:22:43,118
And therefore the women and children would be able to participate in the fighting

306
00:22:43,158 --> 00:22:48,974
 by fighting from the roofs by throwing rocks at the enemy.

307
00:22:50,993 --> 00:22:53,215
And this was the opinion of Rasool Allah ﷺ

308
00:22:53,274 --> 00:22:57,430
and also this was the opinion of Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن ابي), for different reasons.

309
00:22:58,110 --> 00:23:01,560
Rasool Allah ﷺ from a strategic point of view, adopted this opinion.

310
00:23:02,087 --> 00:23:05,089
But Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن ابي) because he was too afraid to go out and fight.

311
00:23:06,100 --> 00:23:12,769
While the majority opinion was to go out and meet the enemy in open field

312
00:23:13,495 --> 00:23:20,212
and their reasoning is that it is shameful for us to hide inside Madina

313
00:23:20,252 --> 00:23:22,696
 and have them come and attack us, in our own home.

314
00:23:23,806 --> 00:23:28,963
But we would go out and meet them and not allow them to even come close to Madina

315
00:23:30,651 --> 00:23:35,363
and this was the opinion of, the ones who did not attend Badr(بدر).

316
00:23:35,943 --> 00:23:38,787
They felt that they missed a lot by not being at Badr(بدر),

317
00:23:38,827 --> 00:23:41,049
so they were so eager to meet the enemy

318
00:23:41,112 --> 00:23:44,372
and they were afraid that if they stay in Madina the enemy wouldn't dare to come in

319
00:23:45,211 --> 00:23:46,657
and they didn't want to miss the Fighting.

320
00:23:48,917 --> 00:23:52,774
And this group, the group who adopted this opinion

321
00:23:52,814 --> 00:23:56,649
put some pressure on Rasool Allah ﷺ until, he agreed to adopt their opinion.

322
00:23:57,895 --> 00:24:02,351
So, he stood up and left the meeting and went inside his house to put on his armor.

323
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:07,153
They felt that they have pressured Rasool Allah ﷺ, so they go to Hamza(حمزه) and say,

324
00:24:08,008 --> 00:24:10,822
go and talk to Rasool Allah ﷺ, we felt that we've pressured him

325
00:24:10,901 --> 00:24:14,327
and we willing to go with what he thinks is, the better opinion.

326
00:24:15,017 --> 00:24:16,395
So, Hamza(حمزه) goes to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

327
00:24:16,435 --> 00:24:18,228
Rasool Allah ﷺ comes out and says;

328
00:24:18,445 --> 00:24:28,308
مَا يَنْبَغِيْ لِنَبِيٍّ اَنْ يَنْزَعْ لَأمة الْحَرْبِ اِذَا وَضَعَهَا حَتَّى يَحْكُمُ الله بَيْنَه’ وَبَيْنَ عَدُّوَّ اَوْ كَمَا قَالَ صَلَّى الله عليه وسلم

329
00:24:29,707 --> 00:24:35,955
Rasool Allah ﷺ, said; It's not appropriate for Prophet, to put on his armor

330
00:24:36,001 --> 00:24:39,930
 and prepare for war, and then take it off

331
00:24:41,431 --> 00:24:44,924
until Allahعَزّوجَلّ judges between him and his enemy.

332
00:24:45,774 --> 00:24:47,428
So, here Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that

333
00:24:47,468 --> 00:24:49,710
we have taken a decision, we're going to go ahead with it,

334
00:24:50,079 --> 00:24:52,619
we're not going to waver, we're not going to change our minds,

335
00:24:52,990 --> 00:24:54,569
we're not going to be indecisive.

336
00:24:54,794 --> 00:24:57,642
If a Prophet make Shura(شورى)

337
00:24:58,232 --> 00:24:59,634
and then takes a decision,

338
00:25:00,285 --> 00:25:01,436
then he will go ahead with it

339
00:25:01,776 --> 00:25:04,494
until Allahعَزّوجَلّ judges between him and his enemy.

340
00:25:04,957 --> 00:25:07,533
I've put this armor on, I'm not going to take it out

341
00:25:07,838 --> 00:25:10,312
until Allahعَزّوجَلّ judges between me and my enemy.

342
00:25:10,686 --> 00:25:13,267
And this is a very important lesson for the leader.

343
00:25:13,676 --> 00:25:18,257
The leader shouldn't be indecisive, the leader shouldn't change his mind every now and then,

344
00:25:18,864 --> 00:25:21,460
the leader shouldn't be wavering back and forth,

345
00:25:21,828 --> 00:25:24,658
according to who spoke to him last.

346
00:25:26,411 --> 00:25:31,134
You make Shura(شورى), you listen to the different opinions , you deliberate,

347
00:25:31,843 --> 00:25:35,449
and then you take a decision, but when you take the decision, it should be final.

348
00:25:37,063 --> 00:25:41,560
Unless there's a change in information,

349
00:25:42,399 --> 00:25:47,346
or the opinion was based on something that turned out to be wrong,

350
00:25:47,827 --> 00:25:49,954
then a person should change.

351
00:25:50,367 --> 00:25:51,985
But if the variables are the same

352
00:25:52,344 --> 00:25:57,171
if the input was the same, nothing changed about it, then why change your mind.

353
00:25:58,286 --> 00:26:01,052
So over here, nothing changed in this situation.

354
00:26:01,243 --> 00:26:05,600
The army is still advancing, it's 3000 strong everything is the same.

355
00:26:05,767 --> 00:26:08,425
And then now the Sahabah(صحابه), some of them changed their mind,

356
00:26:08,472 --> 00:26:13,067
and they're asking Rasool Allah ﷺ and saying, we willing to go with what you think is right.

357
00:26:13,949 --> 00:26:15,286
But it's too late now.

358
00:26:17,339 --> 00:26:23,121
And the followers don't like being led by somebody who is indecisive

359
00:26:24,343 --> 00:26:29,987
And that's something that, especially in War, soldiers don't like that

360
00:26:30,073 --> 00:26:35,207
 because a soldier is putting his life in the hands of his leader,

361
00:26:35,608 --> 00:26:39,106
the Sahabahرضي الله عنهم, their lives are on the line.

362
00:26:39,880 --> 00:26:46,326
And it is Rasool Allah ﷺ who's taking the decision regarding what will directly affect their lives.

363
00:26:47,284 --> 00:26:53,977
So, here Rasool Allah ﷺ is giving an example to every leader, in such a situation

364
00:26:54,350 --> 00:26:56,843
that if you take a decision, it needs to be final.

365
00:26:57,899 --> 00:27:03,600
And there needs to be Samman Ta'ah(سمعاً طاعة), on the side of the followers, the soldiers.

366
00:27:05,151 --> 00:27:07,977
So, they make a decision that they're going to go out and meet the enemy

367
00:27:08,018 --> 00:27:11,069
 and location was Uhud(احد), next to the mountain of Uhud(اُحَدْ).

368
00:27:11,133 --> 00:27:16,408
Uhud(اُحَدْ) is a large mountain few miles outside of Madina.

369
00:27:17,817 --> 00:27:19,689
The Muslim army marches

370
00:27:19,793 --> 00:27:24,461
 but Rasool Allah ﷺ told the Sahabah(صحابه) can any one of you, guide us through a way

371
00:27:25,127 --> 00:27:30,303
that will bring us out to the enemy without them Realizing.

372
00:27:31,554 --> 00:27:33,265
So, Abu Khaisamah(ابوخيثمه) said: I will.

373
00:27:34,097 --> 00:27:38,455
And they travel through agricultural land

374
00:27:39,378 --> 00:27:43,133
rather than the traditional routes that lead out of Madina.

375
00:27:44,485 --> 00:27:51,643
And they pass through a farm owned by one of Al-Munafiqeen(منافقين), Mirbah Bin Qaidhee(مربع بن قيضي).

376
00:27:53,200 --> 00:27:54,838
So, when they were walking through his farm,

377
00:27:54,878 --> 00:27:59,238
obviously when an army is walking through agricultural land

378
00:28:00,342 --> 00:28:03,610
it's unavoidable that there will be some damage.

379
00:28:04,692 --> 00:28:09,172
So, Mirbah Bin Qaidhee(مربع بن قيضي) wanted to stop the Muslim army and he was blind.

380
00:28:10,573 --> 00:28:15,521
So, he said; If you are the messenger of Allah, than I do not permit you to enter my garden,

381
00:28:16,188 --> 00:28:17,441
I don't allow it to come through,

382
00:28:17,723 --> 00:28:18,867
you're trespassing,

383
00:28:19,312 --> 00:28:27,174
if you come through my farm or consider it trespassing you are destroying my property.

384
00:28:28,459 --> 00:28:32,248
But Rasool Allah ﷺ ignores him and the Army goes forward.

385
00:28:32,567 --> 00:28:35,115
 So, he picks up some dirt in his hand and he said;

386
00:28:35,773 --> 00:28:41,821
